<p>The World Health Organization declared an Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo and Uganda a public health emergency of international concern, saying the outbreak caused by Bundibugyo virus does not meet the criteria for a pandemic emergency. WHO said the designation followed confirmed cross-border transmission and rising suspected cases. As of May 16, WHO said DRC’s Ituri province had reported eight laboratory-confirmed cases, 246 suspected cases and 80 suspected deaths, while Uganda had reported two laboratory-confirmed cases in Kampala, including one death, in people who had traveled from DRC. Separate media reports gave different tallies: more than 300 suspected cases, or 336 suspected cases and 88 deaths. Reports also described spread beyond the initial Ituri cluster. WHO called the outbreak &quot;extraordinary&quot; because Bundibugyo virus has no approved virus-specific vaccine or treatment and countries bordering DRC face a high risk of further spread. The agency advised emergency management preparations but did not recommend closing international borders.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4mqVTgr89Dw19UEs8TZK_rnXwLnALcjnHIFdB-BK-hJ4pNictmpZgJglhIcLLOGwwwBu4ytnyTjHbDbHDdrjQHmsG7b3qqrwXRS67LtzdJGd-g4uw04iRM8KO6qQx3dC9A6e6u24di25ykDXQlBpABNc589_C-IfMvy8GO5ChDul7jDBWdLqIlDPjVBI1oNC7n4WnnogFYiFlGHw0X2nm-a5nOTleGhvt77C6lo-6pyc0szjk-mrVnKHLytK8vZow70kLRilP4lsITeSNg' alt='A motorcycle taxi driver waits outside CBCA Virunga General Hospital in Goma, where a first Ebola case was reported during the outbreak.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Decision process: Politico reported that Tedros made the emergency determination himself, rather than through WHO’s usual expert committee process, after consulting DRC and Uganda.</li><li>Capital case: A laboratory-confirmed case in Kinshasa involved a person returning from Ituri, placing the virus in a capital city far from the initial cluster.</li><li>Humanitarian backdrop: Al Jazeera described the outbreak as a deadly Ebola resurgence in northeastern DRC amid a worsening humanitarian crisis.</li><li>Kampala link gap: WHO said the two confirmed Kampala cases had recently traveled from DRC but had no established direct epidemiological link, raising concern about undetected transmission.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus: He thanked the governments of DRC and Uganda for their commitment and for sharing risk assessments, which WHO said allowed other countries to take preparedness measures. (<a href='https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern'>WHO</a>)</li><li>Bloomberg: The outlet described WHO’s declaration as a step aimed at spurring a broader global response to the outbreak. (<a href='https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-05-17/who-declares-congo-uganda-ebola-outbreak-global-health-emergency'>Bloomberg</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3353866/ebola-outbreak-dr-congo-uganda-declared-international-health-emergency'>Ebola outbreak in DR Congo, Uganda declared an international health emergency</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/aa55ba2b-8476-4718-8d28-5f60df6ff19c'>WHO declares global health emergency on Ebola</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2l2p0wwzzdo'>WHO declares Ebola outbreak in DR Congo an international emergency</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/who-declares-global-health-emergency-over-ebola-outbreak/'>WHO declares global health emergency over Ebola outbreak</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/congo-ebola-outbreak-dead-usaid-response/'>Ebola outbreak in Congo and Uganda declared global health emergency</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/who-declares-